    "template": "ChatGPT prompt engineering toolkit\n\nPromptmetheus Features:\n\nPromptmetheus is a development platform designed to assist users in constructing, testing, and assessing one-shot prompts for the OpenAI platform. The platform allows users to generate dedicated AIPIs (AI Programming Interfaces) for their applications, utilizing ChatGPT and other Large Language Models (LLMs) to their full potential.\n\nKey Features:\n\n– Build prompts using allocated blocks and fragments.– Test and compare different models and input parameters.– Rate, organize, search, and filter prompt outputs.– Predicted cost per prompt execution.– Performance visualization of prompts and fragments.– Data export capabilities such as .csv, .xlsx, or .json file formats.\n\nFAQs:\n\n– An AIPI is similar to a traditional API, but it communicates with AI models instead of applications.– One-shot prompts provide predictable output based on a single request, making them crucial for integrating prompt responses into products or automated workflows.– Support for GPT-4 is available.– Users do not necessitate developer credentials to utilize Promptmetheus as ChatGPT interactions only demand reading and writing abilities.– Promptmetheus is not open-source.– Data is stored in the user’s browser, with no database established.– Users pay for OpenAI API usage with their provided API key.– Promptmetheus is a cost-free platform that enables users to employ AI to their applications.",
